// EduFlow Prisma schema — DEFERRED.
//
// The ERD (ARC-01 / Prompt Pack P4) has not been written. The owner has
// deferred it, so no schema is guessed here.
//
// WHY THIS FILE IS EMPTY RATHER THAN PARTIAL
// -----------------------------------------
// A plausible-looking but invented schema is worse than none. Entity
// shapes are the thing AGENTS.md 6 warns about: "creating a parallel
// concept under a new name is the most common way this codebase drifts."
// A guessed `Student` or `Class` written now would have to be reconciled
// against the real ERD later, and a reviewer would have to decide which
// of the two was right.
//
// CONSTRAINTS THAT WILL APPLY WHEN IT IS WRITTEN
// ----------------------------------------------
//   - PostgreSQL only. SQLite is not an option (ADR-003, one database
//     per school; and money needs real numerics — ADR-002).
//   - Money is integer minor units + explicit currency. Never float.
//   - school_id is carried as METADATA, not a security control
//     (AGENTS.md 2.1). Do not build tenant scoping. Do not add a
//     cross-tenant role.
//   - Uniqueness is scoped within one school's database. A global
//     @unique would be wrong, not merely redundant.
//   - audit_records has UPDATE and DELETE revoked from the application
//     role (AGENTS.md 2.7, PLT-401).
//
// The API runs with persistence DISABLED until this file exists — see
// src/config/env.ts, which makes that state explicit rather than silent.

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
}
